   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Finland added the most: $88 more per person on heritage than before the pandemic** ($177 in 2019, $265 in 2023). The biggest increases:\n\n- **Finland:** +$88 a person\n- **Switzerland:** +$56 a person\n- **Slovakia:** +$28 a person\n- **Ecuador:** +$25 a person\n- **Canada:** +$25 a person\n\nOf the 31 countries with figures for both periods, 17 spend more than before the pandemic; a map beside the dashboard shows where spending rose and fell. Public spending per person in constant 2017 purchasing-power dollars. Source: UIS, February 2026 release; indicator HEXPCSTPPPCAP.HER.PU.",
